  "summary": "Risk-off sentiment grips markets as surging oil prices from Middle East tensions pressure US equities. Bitcoin shows unusual strength, decoupling from the broader macro trend and suggesting strong intrinsic demand. Gold remains neutral, caught between safe-haven flows and a stronger dollar.",
  "morning_report": "The primary market driver is the escalating conflict in the Middle East, which has sent oil prices surging. This has had a direct negative impact on US equities, with both the Nasdaq and S&P 500 selling off on inflation and economic slowdown fears. In contrast, Bitcoin has rallied towards $72,000, indicating its current price action is being driven more by crypto-specific factors than the macro environment. Gold is treading water, with its safe-haven appeal being offset by a stronger dollar fueled by dimmed hopes for near-term rate cuts.",
